# Phase 7 — Proof-of-Scholarship

This is the human layer and arguably the eventual moat.

A scholar does not simply click:

```text
👍
```

They issue a typed judgment against an exact version:

```text
ReviewEvent
├── reviewer identity
├── credentials / expertise scope
├── exact object/version
├── decision
│   ACCEPT
│   REVISE
│   REJECT
│   ABSTAIN
├── judgment scope
│   philology
│   morphology
│   translation
│   argument
│   historical claim
│   etc.
├── reasoning
├── references
├── confidence/limitations
└── timestamp/signature
```

This produces what you were calling **Proof-of-Scholarship**.

The scarce asset is not the scholar's name sitting on a PDF.

It's:

> **an attributable expert judgment on an exact versioned claim, with its domain of competence and downstream consequence recorded.**

Then authority is multidimensional:

```text
generated_by_model
engineering_verified
machine_evaluated
published_scholar_corroborated
specialist_reviewed
independently_reviewed
adjudicated
```

No single fake “confidence score.”

